WP01 security and no-overclaim proof

Covered by app-game.test.ts:
- Display-name-only identity stays weak, unlinked, and low-confidence.
- Inventory evidence cannot claim running state.
- Inventory evidence cannot claim foreground state.
- Launcher evidence cannot become knownGame without child-game proof.
- AI classification digest cannot carry terminate or other enforcement authority.

Covered by app-game-control-authority.test.ts:
- Observer/read-only authority cannot approve, deny, extend, or override.
- Approval requests require evidence references.
- Game policy cannot point at /appPolicy write paths.
- Manual-required capability cannot claim strict execution.
- Launcher-only game proof cannot become dispatch-ready gameplay proof.
- Unknown app proof cannot become dispatch-ready app control proof.
- Denied approval decisions cannot still claim enforcement.

Not in this slice:
- No child-device runtime adapter executed.
- No portal UI rendered app/game rows.
- No Rust service or SQLite journal behavior changed.
